Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Fallback for Wine builds WITHOUT the wine-staging "loader-KeyboardLayouts" patch
; (Wine bug 47439). Upstream Wine's registry template has no
; HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Keyboard Layouts keys at all, and .NET
; Framework's InputLanguage.LayoutName opens "<Keyboard Layouts>\00000409" and calls
; GetValue on it with no null check, so it throws NullReferenceException when the key
; is missing. libpalaso reads LayoutName on the same line as Culture, so this is the
; next crash after the culture one on a plain (non-staging) Wine >= 11.2.
;
; Not needed on wine-staging based runners (e.g. kron4ek-wine-11.x-staging), which
; create these keys (empty) themselves.
;
; Import into a Bottles bottle:  bottle > Tools > Registry editor > File > Import
; or, for a plain prefix:        wine regedit /path/to/keyboard-layouts-00000409.reg

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Keyboard Layouts]

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Keyboard Layouts\00000409]
"Layout File"="KBDUS.DLL"
"Layout Text"="US"
